# Architecture Diagram Template

Purpose:
  Template for architecture diagrams accompanying API implementations.
  Every API implementation MUST include a diagram showing the data flow,
  entry point, dependencies, and fallback paths. Stored alongside the CASE spec.

Owns: templates/_sdd/architecture/DIAGRAM-TEMPLATE.sdd

## Diagram Requirements

Every implementation diagram MUST include:

  1. Entry point — how the API is invoked
  2. Data flow — direction and medium (HTTP, queue, DB)
  3. Dependencies — what this component depends on
  4. Fallback paths — what happens on failure
  5. Why — business or technical rationale

## Format

Mermaid Diagram-as-Code (C4 model):

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "API Layer"
        CLIENT[Client] -->|HTTP POST| API[Endpoint Handler]
    end

    subgraph "Business Logic"
        API --> SVC[PaymentService]
        SVC --> REPO[PaymentRepository]
    end

    subgraph "External"
        SVC -->|provider API| PROVIDER[Payment Provider]
        SVC -->|event| OUTBOX[Outbox]
    end

    subgraph "Fallback"
        PROVIDER -- "on failure" --> DLQ[Dead Letter Queue]
    end

    STYLE API fill:#4a90d9,stroke:#fff,color:#fff
```

## Why-How-What Documentation

After the diagram, include:

  WHY: <business or technical reason for this approach>

  HOW: <key implementation mechanism>

  WHAT: <what data/entities are affected>

## Example Placement

  File location:
    .sdd/projects/{project_name}/architecture/diagrams/CASE_02_03-diagram.md

  Reference from CASE spec:
    See: @projects/{project_name}/architecture/diagrams/CASE_02_03-diagram.md

## Rules

  [D1] Every API implementation MUST have a diagram.
  [D2] Diagrams MUST be in Mermaid format.
  [D3] C4 model is preferred (Context, Containers, Components, Code).
  [D4] Fallback paths MUST be documented.
  [D5] Diagrams MUST be checked into the architecture/diagrams/ directory.
  [D6] Diagrams MUST be referenced from the CASE spec that owns the API.

State: +
